#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:116
msgid ""
"The associated records (`spawnOptions`, `childProcess<'o>`, "
"`terminatedPayload`) are re-exported from `PluginShell`. See [`packages"
"/plugin-shell/src/PluginShell.resi`](https://github.com/Nagatatz"
"/rescript-tauri/tree/main/packages/plugin-shell/src/PluginShell.resi) for"
" the full doc comments and matching upstream URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:121
msgid "Running commands"
msgstr "コマンド実行"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:123
msgid "One-shot execution"
msgstr "ワンショット実行"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:125
msgid ""
"`Command.execute` resolves once the child has exited and gives you the "
"collected output. Best for short-lived commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:138
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`childProcess<'o>` carries `{code, signal, stdout, stderr}`. Both `code` "
"and `signal` are `Nullable.t<int>` — they're mutually exclusive on Unix "
"(signal-terminated processes report `code = null`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:142
msgid "Background processes"
msgstr "バックグラウンドプロセス"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:144
msgid ""
"`Command.spawn` starts the child and returns a `Child.t` handle without "
"waiting. Combine it with `Child.write` and `Child.kill` for interactive "
"use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:158
msgid "`Child.pid` returns the OS-level process id."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:160
msgid "Raw byte output"
msgstr "Raw byte 出力"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:162
msgid ""
"Pass `encoding: \"raw\"` via the dedicated factory functions to receive "
"`Uint8Array.t` instead of `string`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:173
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The TypeScript-level conditional return type of upstream's "
"`Command.create({encoding: 'raw'})` is split into four ReScript functions"
" — `Command.create` / `Command.createRaw` / `Command.sidecar` / "
"`Command.sidecarRaw` — so the result type is always statically known."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:179
msgid "Streaming output"
msgstr "ストリーミング出力"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:181
msgid ""
"Use chained `onStdoutData` / `onStderrData` / `onClose` / `onError` to "
"stream events from a long-running command. Each method returns the "
"command, mirroring the upstream `Promise<this>` pattern:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:205
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For advanced subscription patterns (`once`, `prependListener`, manual "
"`listenerCount`, ...) reach for `Command.stdout` / `Command.stderr` "
"directly — both return an `EventEmitter.t<{\"data\": 'o}>` you can drive "
"with the `EventEmitter` module's 9 generic methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:211
msgid ""
"`Command.removeAllListeners` detaches every command-level listener "
"(`close` / `error`). To clear stdout / stderr listeners, use "
"`EventEmitter.removeAllListeners` on the corresponding accessor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:216
msgid "Sidecar binaries"
msgstr "Sidecar バイナリ"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:218
msgid ""
"Sidecars are binaries bundled alongside your app and looked up through "
"`tauri.conf.json > bundle > externalBin` instead of `PATH`. Use "
"`Command.sidecar` (or `sidecarRaw` for bytes):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:230
msgid ""
"The string passed to `sidecar` matches the `externalBin` entry without "
"the target triple suffix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:233
msgid "Opening paths and URLs"
msgstr "パス / URL を開く"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:235
msgid "`openPath` opens its argument with the system's default application:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:243
msgid ""
"Pass `~openWith` to force a specific opener (`firefox`, `chromium`, "
"`safari`, `xdg-open`, ...). The path or URL must match a `shell:allow-"
"open` regex — otherwise the underlying call rejects:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:252
msgid "Pitfalls"
msgstr "注意点"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:254
msgid "`openPath` rename"
msgstr "`openPath` へのリネーム"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:256
msgid ""
"Upstream exposes this function as `open`, but ReScript reserves that "
"identifier for module access (`open MyModule`). We re-export it as "
"`openPath`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:268
msgid "`Uint8Array` length"
msgstr "`Uint8Array` の長さ取得"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:270
msgid ""
"`Uint8Array.t` in `@rescript/core` is an alias for `TypedArray.t<int>`. "
"The length getter lives on the parent module:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:279
msgid "Scope misconfiguration"
msgstr "Scope 設定ミス"

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:281
msgid ""
"Commands fail to spawn — and `openPath` fails to launch — when the target"
" is not allowlisted in `src-tauri/capabilities/`. The `name` field on "
"`shell:allow-execute` must match the first argument to `Command.create` /"
" `Command.sidecar` exactly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-shell.md:293
msgid ""
"`Command.create(\"git\", ...)` then succeeds; `Command.create(\"Git\", "
"...)` or `Command.create(\"/usr/bin/git\", ...)` rejects."
msgstr ""

